 "intro_zh": "贫困点纪念性土方工程得名于该地点附近的一座 19 世纪种植园，该种植园位于密西西比河下游流域，地势略高且狭窄。该建筑群由五个土丘、六个被浅洼地隔开的同心半椭圆形山脊和一个中央广场组成。它是由一个狩猎渔民社会在距今 3700 至 3100 年间建造并用于居住和仪式目的。这是北美土建筑的一项了不起的成就，至少 2000 年来无人能超越。",
 "intro_zh_source": "machine_translation",
 "intro_en": "Monumental Earthworks of Poverty Point owes its name to a 19th-century plantation close to the site, which is in the Lower Mississippi Valley on a slightly elevated and narrow landform. The complex comprises five mounds, six concentric semi-elliptical ridges separated by shallow depressions and a central plaza. It was created and used for residential and ceremonial purposes by a society of hunter fisher-gatherers between 3700 and 3100 BP. It is a remarkable achievement in earthen construction in North America that was unsurpassed for at least 2,000 years.",
 "intro_en_source": "unesco_official",
